            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0639" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51/336: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-01T10:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                                1924—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 1—8:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. James Grant Forbes, representing Blair and Company, New York, has arrived in
                    Teheran to study Persia’s securities for loan of $10,000,000 provided in
                    Sinclair contract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
